    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "## Bug\n\n`AuthStatus()` for the Agy (Antigravity) adapter always returns `Unknown` once the binary resolves, regardless of whether the user is actually authenticated. This is a real, live-verified gap distinct from the model-catalog work in [#3385](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/issues/3385)/[PR #3386](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/pull/3386) (merged) and [PR #3960](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/pull/3960) (open, fixes an Agy model-discovery pipe-drain bug) \u2014 those cover model discovery, not auth detection.\n\n**Source:** live reproduction on a user's machine via Claude Code session | **Analyzed against:** `main` @ current HEAD (fetched directly, confirmed unchanged from the fork checkout) | **Reported by:** @Hendrixx-RE\n**Confidence:** High\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`backend/internal/adapters/agent/agy/auth.go`:\n\n```go\nfunc (p *Plugin) AuthStatus(ctx context.Context) (ports.AgentAuthStatus, error) {\n\tif _, err := p.ResolveBinary(ctx); err != nil {\n\t\treturn ports.AgentAuthStatusUnknown, err\n\t}\n\t// Antigravity authenticates through its OS keyring and browser sign-in. The\n\t// official CLI does not expose a documented non-interactive credential file\n\t// or status command, so local auth cannot safely be inferred here.\n\treturn ports.AgentAuthStatusUnknown, nil\n}\n```\n\nThe comment's premise is out of date: the real `agy` CLI (confirmed real binary, `agy --version` \u2192 `1.1.22`) has a documented `models` subcommand that already IS used for model discovery elsewhere in the codebase (`backend/internal/adapters/agent/modelcatalog/catalog.go`: `\"agy\": {args: []string{\"models\"}, parser: parseIDLines}`). Running it directly:\n\n```\n$ agy models\nFetching available models...\ngemini-3.7-flash-high\tGemini 3.7 Flash (High)\n...\nclaude-opus-4-6-thinking\tClaude Opus 4.6 (Thinking)\n```\n\nsucceeds non-interactively with no login prompt when the user is authenticated (it fetches live data from a remote service). A successful `agy models` call (which AO already runs for the model catalog) is a usable, already-computed signal of auth state \u2014 but `AuthStatus()` doesn't consult it, or any other signal, and unconditionally reports `Unknown`.\n\n## Impact\n\nEvery Agy/Antigravity user sees an uninformative \"unknown\" auth indicator in AO's UI regardless of actual login state, with no way to distinguish \"not logged in, spawn will fail\" from \"logged in and ready.\" This surfaced in the wild as \"AO can't detect my Antigravity auth.\"\n\n## Suggested Fix\n\n`AuthStatus()` could reuse the model-catalog discovery call (or a cheap equivalent) as a proxy signal: a successful `agy models` call implies authenticated; a failure that looks like an auth/login prompt implies not authenticated. Since the model catalog fetch (`modelcatalog` package) already runs this exact command and caches results, `AuthStatus()` may be able to piggyback on that cache instead of shelling out separately, avoiding duplicate CLI invocations.\n\n## Related\n\n- [#3385](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/issues/3385) \u2014 adapter-aware model selection RFC, merged via [PR #3386](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/pull/3386); covers model discovery for Agy, not auth.\n- [PR #3960](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/pull/3960) \u2014 open, fixes an Agy-specific model-discovery pipe-drain timeout bug; same subsystem, different bug.\n- [#4031](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/issues/4031) \u2014 same class of problem for a different adapter (\"bug(kimi): OAuth-managed auth is reported unknown or unauthorized\").",
